            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for suggestion!\r\n\r\nWell, it is interesting and in theory not that hard to implement. I am more worried about inherited complexity that might come with it. It seems to be more useful for these lists to have both \"local\" and \"global\" nature. That means a need for a check on every cursor movement, which is not a great news for execution speed.\r\n\r\nI'll think about it, but at the moment my expectation is not that high.",
